# dbus -- the bus every part of GNOME talks over. gnome-session, gnome-shell,
# gsd, gdm, polkit and elogind are all D-Bus services first and programs second.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://dbus.freedesktop.org/releases/dbus/dbus-1.16.2.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=0ba2a1a4b16afe7bceb2c07e9ce99a8c2c3508e5dec290dbb643384bd6beb7e2
SRC_DIR=dbus-1.16.2

# systemd=disabled: there is none, and with it enabled dbus installs unit files
# and expects to be socket-activated.
#
# x11_autolaunch=disabled: it exists so a D-Bus client with no session bus can
# start one via an X display. Duct's session is Wayland and the X libraries are
# not present this early in the order, so the fallback could not work anyway.
#
# The three documentation toggles are off because doxygen, ducktype and the
# docbook stylesheets are none of them packaged; with them on auto, meson finds
# them missing and fails rather than skipping.
MESON_ARGS="-Dsystemd=disabled -Dselinux=disabled -Dapparmor=disabled \
-Dlibaudit=disabled -Dx11_autolaunch=disabled -Dmodular_tests=disabled \
-Ddoxygen_docs=disabled -Dducktype_docs=disabled -Dxml_docs=disabled \
-Dsession_socket_dir=/tmp -Druntime_dir=/run -Dsystem_pid_file=/run/dbus/pid \
-Dsystem_socket=/run/dbus/system_bus_socket -Ddbus_user=messagebus"
